.SH "Field Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int32_t(* schultz_widget_vtable::paint) (\fBschultz_tree\fP *tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_draw_list\fP *list, \fBschultz_arena\fP *arena)"
Appends this node's drawing to the frame's command list\&.
.PP
Called with the node's absolute bounds already computed and any clip already pushed\&. Coordinates are in window space, so a widget positions itself from schultz_node_absolute_bounds rather than assuming an origin\&.
.PP
The arena is per frame scratch and is reset before the next one, so anything allocated from it must not be kept\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB225\fP of file \fBschultz_widget\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "int32_t(* schultz_widget_vtable::event) (\fBschultz_tree\fP *tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const \fBschultz_event\fP *event)"
Handles an event aimed at this node, before the host sees it\&.
.PP
Returning nonzero consumes the event and stops it reaching the host, which is what a text field does with a keystroke\&. Returning zero lets it through, which is what a button does with its click\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB235\fP of file \fBschultz_widget\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "int32_t(* schultz_widget_vtable::tick) (\fBschultz_tree\fP *tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint64_t now_ms, uint32_t elapsed_ms)"
Moves this node on by however long has passed\&.
.PP
Called from schultz_tree_advance, and only for nodes that asked to be ticked with schultz_node_set_animating\&. Nothing else in the toolkit knows what time it is, so this is where anything that changes on its own rather than in answer to input does its changing\&.
.PP
Return nonzero when something changed and the node needs painting again\&. A widget that has nothing to do this tick returns zero, and the frame costs nothing\&. 
.PP
